t them, and the Sign button stays off.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When your terms are ready, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>. Everything is filled in from your application: check the short list of key values (each has a <b class="gd-ui">Fix</b> link) and open any document to read it in full.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: say you read the documents, initial the three confirmations, tick the two consents and draw your signature. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Sign all</b>. A code to your phone or email is optional (<b class="gd-ui">Verify by code</b>); it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on. One signature covers every document, in about two minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Pay the upfront invoice: the first and last month&#39;s insurance fee for each car (see chapter 4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what each car&#39;s checklist asks for: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission if it is financed or leased, and insurance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Sign Forms C and D (filled in for you) on screen, with your witnesses beside you on the same device: Form C with one witness, Form D with two (see chapter 5).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-if-we-need-a-little-more" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we need a little more</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes we need one more document before we can approve your application, for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an email, and Home shows &quot;We need a little more&quot; with the list and any note from our team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what is asked, or write Your answer, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send my answer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We review it within 1 business day. Once we approve your application, you get an email and Home shows Check and sign.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No typing the VIN: press <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and point your phone at the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b> and take a photo of it. Check the VIN shown before you continue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Photos:</b> on your car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> takes any number at once, in any order. We sort them, put the outside photos on our studio background and touch up the inside ones. Photos that fit no shot go in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>. At least 10 are needed.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-a-fleet-supplier-lease-your-cars-to-carmacars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</h2><p class="gd-p">For a corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars for a fixed amount a month. You pay CarmaCars no fees: no invoices, no debits.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span> and press <b class="gd-ui">A corporation with a fleet? Lease your cars to us as a fleet supplier</b> (or choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b> in the application, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">About you: the corporation&#39;s legal name and number, its registered address, and the signing officer&#39;s name and title.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For each car: type the VIN (the year, make and model fill in), then the plate, and mark the car <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it needs work). Each tier shows its lease a month. The tier is set when you add the car and does not change.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Say who the car is registered to now: <b class="gd-ui">My corporation</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Me or another officer, personally</b> (it moves into your corporation), or <b class="gd-ui">A seller: the corporation is buying it</b>. For the last two, enter the name and address on the ownership and the transfer or sale date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>, check the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Submit application</b>. The ServiceOntario forms each car needs are filled in for you at once, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: the lease to CarmaCars (CarmaCars holds the plates while it leases the car) and, for a car not yet registered to your corporation, the transfer into it. A seller signs the transfer on the back of the ownership. Only the empty boxes are filled. Sign each one on screen under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, then print it and sign it in ink at ServiceOntario.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">In your owner portal, open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then each car, and upload its ownership (registration) copy.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option). Form D (the limited power of attorney) is in your Documents too: you sign it on screen with two witnesses beside you, and CarmaCars signs its Part 2 at the same moment.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Home and <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> show <b class="gd-ui">Your fleet lease</b>: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">You sign your agreement before any car comes over. As soon as your profile has your legal or corporation name, your address and, for a corporation, the signing officer and title, your agreement is made from it: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement (with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement it relies on) if you lease cars to CarmaCars, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. No car is needed.</p><p class="gd-p">Your owner portal home shows six steps: Your profile, Sign the agreement, Add your cars, Photos and inspection, Approved, Delivered. The current step has one button; press it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement.</b> Read and sign opens it, filled in from your profile. You sign once on screen; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Add your cars.</b> One at a time, or as a list of VINs from Cars &gt; Add cars from a VIN list (a fleet supplier gives each car its tier and plate there). Each car goes on Schedule A of your agreement as a numbered entry, and you confirm each batch with one signature (Confirm my cars). Its government forms are made at the same moment.</li><li>A car is approved, delivered or rented only once your agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. If CarmaCars approved it before you signed, it goes through by itself the moment you sign.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'documents-and-forms', 'chapter', 'rewards', 'Your signed agreements, uploads and government forms are under Documents. Some forms are filled for you; Forms C and D are signed on screen with your witnesses beside you.

## Sign everything at once

Everything you sign on screen is in one place: Home shows how many are signed ("2 of 5 signed") and opens it with Check and sign.

1. Press **Check and sign** on Home (or open `carmacars.ca/owner/sign`). The list at the top shows each document: signed, in this package, or done elsewhere (Forms C and D, the bank debit).
2. Check the key values: your name, address, each car with its VIN and plate, your fees and Revenue Share. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it, change it, and come back.
3. Open any document to read it word for word: the agreements, the schedules and Forms A and B. The official registry forms are not in it: they are printed and signed in ink.
4. A code is optional: press **Verify by code** if you want the certificate to say a 6-digit code to your phone or email confirmed it was you (it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on).
5. Tick that you read the documents, draw your initials in the box beside each confirmation the Enrollment Agreement asks for, and tick the two consents (to sign electronically, to get your records electronically).
6. Draw your signature in the box with your finger, a pen or the mouse, then press **Sign all**. One signature is applied to each document; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment and every signed copy is in Documents.
7. Each signed copy ends with a certificate of completion: when and where each step was done, and whether a code confirmed it was you. Anyone holding a copy can check it at carmacars.ca/verify.

## Read your agreements before approval

You can read both agreements as soon as you apply, before we approve your terms.

1. Press **Read your agreements** on Home (Documents and each car''s Onboarding checklist link to it too).
2. Each document is filled in from your application: your name, address and cars. It is marked "Terms pending approval": the fees, the Revenue Share and the agreement numbers read Pending approval until we set them.
3. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it. The Sign button stays off until we approve your terms; then Home shows **Check and sign** and we email you.

> Two owners: A car with a second owner on its ownership? Each owner named in the Title Schedule signs. The other owner gets their own link by email and signs the same documents on their phone or computer, the same way: the documents read, the confirmations initialled, the consents and their drawn signature (a code to their email only if they choose it or CarmaCars turns it on). The agreements take effect when the last owner signs; CarmaCars countersigns then.

> Good to know: Cannot draw a signature (for example with a disability)? Call us: an Admin can let you type your name instead.

> Good to know: Form A (the trust declaration) is for cars under the Co-Registrant or Transfer method; Form B (the lease summary) for cars under a Lease method. No witness is needed: they are in the same package. You can also sign one on its own page from Documents.

> Good to know: Every agreement is signed on screen, with the e-signature. A copy signed on paper is not accepted (a document you signed on paper before November 2026 stays on file as Signed on paper).

## We set up your car for you

When our team enters your car for you, you get one email: review the details and sign.

1. No sign-in yet? The email has a link to choose your password. It works once, for 24 hours; after that use Forgot password on the sign-in page.
2. Open `carmacars.ca/owner/review` (Home has **Review or correct your details**). Check your phone and address, and each car: plate, colour, odometer, your insurer and your lender. The terms we agreed are shown too.
3. Something wrong? Correct it and press **Save corrections**. Your documents are filled in again and we are told. A term you did not agree to: message us before you sign.
4. Everything right? Press **Everything is right: sign** and sign once.

## Sign an updated Vehicle Schedule

When we agree new terms for a car you already signed for, you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. Home shows it first.

1. Open it from Home or the email. It shows what changes (now and updated) and the date it applies from.
2. Read the text, then sign the same way as your agreements: tick that you read it, initial the updated terms, tick the two consents, draw your signature and press **Sign** (a code to your phone or email is optional).
3. Your current terms stay until you sign. After that, your invoices and statements use the new ones from the date. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is in Documents.

## Form C on screen, with your witness beside you

Form C is the lender or lessor permission for a financed or leased car. It needs one witness, and you can sign it on screen when your witness is with you.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press **Sign Form C on screen**.
2. Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on).
3. Draw your initials beside each of the three acknowledgments, tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Hand the device to your witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement "I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence." Press **Sign Form C**.

![](/guides/img/owner-16-form-c-screen-desktop-faa92983.jpg "desktop; size: 790 980; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/form-c/4898eb96-0cce-4efc-9fdd-740b4b4e9ad3; pins: 2 5.7 13.6, 3 32.9 55.1, 4 6.3 82.2")

## Form D on screen, with your two witnesses beside you

Form D is a limited power of attorney, once for all your cars. It needs two witnesses, and you sign it on screen with both of them beside you.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press **Sign Form D on screen**.
2. Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
3. Hand the device to your first witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement "I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence." Then the same for your second witness.
4. Press **Sign Form D**. CarmaCars signs Part 2 at the same moment, and the signed copy is in Documents.

> Good to know: A paper copy is no longer accepted: Forms C and D are signed on screen only. A form you sent as a photo before November 2026 stays on file.

## Government forms filled for you

Each car''s registry forms are filled in by themselves from your records as soon as its terms are approved, only the ones its onboarding method needs (013-1155 and 013-0169, for example, only for a Lease through a new corporation). When you add a missing value (your address, the odometer) they are filled in again by themselves. Until we load the official PDF, you get a data sheet with the values.

Open **Documents**: the **Government forms** box lists each one with its status and the date it was made. If we correct a value on a form before you sign it, the form is made again and Documents always shows the current one.

1. Open Documents. Each form shows **Signed** or **Not signed**. Press **Sign** next to a form, or **Check and sign** on Home (the government forms are one To do on your Onboarding checklist).
2. Each form is the official ServiceOntario form, exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it, with only its empty text boxes filled in. Press **Show the form**, check every value and tick that you checked it. Do this for each form.
3. Tick that you read the form, give the two consents and draw your signature. CarmaCars records one signature for each form, with the date, your IP address and your device.
4. Press **Sign the form** (or **Sign the 3 forms**). When every form is signed, the step is done.
5. Then press **Download the filled form** on a form, print it and sign it in ink. Its boxes to tick and its signatures are done by hand, at the registry office or before you go, as we tell you.

If a value on a form changes after you signed it (we correct your address, for example), Documents shows **Changed since signed**, Home shows one To do to sign it again, and we send you one reminder email. Your earlier signature stays on record.

![](/guides/img/owner-13-official-form-desktop-48614913.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 732; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/forms/4d54a524-c28d-4bc4-8ad3-dd9558100a81/official; pins: 2 22.2 29.5")

> Good to know: ON00453 (a company''s registrant number) is an Adobe form: open it in Adobe Acrobat Reader (free) to see and print it. Other PDF viewers show a blank page, as they do with the form downloaded from ServiceOntario.

> Watch out: Your on-screen signature is a record that you agree to the values on the form. It is never put on the official form: the printed form has no signature until you sign it in ink. You pay ServiceOntario, the inspection station and the appraiser directly.

## The agreement for your deal

Your agreement is filled in from the terms we agreed with you. We email you a link when it is ready: **Read and sign** opens it in your portal, and you sign once for every document.

1. **Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement**: if your corporation leases cars to CarmaCars. It lists each car with its tier (Regular or Troubled), its monthly lease and its delivery date. Each car''s tier is set once, when it is delivered. You pay CarmaCars no fees. We pay in arrears on the 10th: a car''s first payment comes one full month after delivery, and part months are paid by the day, with the calculation on your statement.
2. **Referral Override Agreement**: if you referred another owner. It sets the override we pay you on their cars (out of our share, never theirs) and what you can see of those cars. Find it under **Cars**: Sign your Referral Override Agreement.
3. Something wrong in it? Reply to the email before you sign and we fix it.
', 'Documents and forms', 'Agreements, government forms, Forms C and D, and official forms filled for you.',
