  '<p class="gd-p">Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b>. Every owner application, newest first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open an application to decide.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.8%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.8%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-decide-on-an-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decide on an application</h2><p class="gd-p">One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the driver&#39;s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The step &quot;Terms and first invoice&quot; opens for each car, filled in with the owner&#39;s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, <b class="gd-ui">Use these terms for every car</b> copies the first car&#39;s numbers to the others.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Missing something? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for something</b>, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the owner</b>. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Not a fit? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, write the Reason the owner reads, and press <b class="gd-ui">Decline the application</b>. The owner is emailed for each car.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.9%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:49.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says &quot;Entered by staff&quot; and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Notes on the page are for staff only: <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b> keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> tab, or <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on an owner&#39;s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner&#39;s terms, or their other car&#39;s; change them for this car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and set it up</b>. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, <b class="gd-ui">Send the set-up email again</b> sends the owner the email with a fresh link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b> shows their portal. <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> helps them sign in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send invitation</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.4%;top:49.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:82.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer&#39;s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-mark-a-car-insured-insurer-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: &quot;Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured&quot;. It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the insurer&#39;s email arrives, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark insured</b>. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer&#39;s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One email for several cars? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark several insured</b> on the line &quot; cars wait for the insurer&quot;. Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same button is on the car: Overview (<b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>) and the Listing tab&#39;s checklist, item &quot;Not on the fleet insurance policy yet&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email &quot;Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy&quot;. Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners-who-paid-another-way-and-the-terms-you-agreed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed</h2><p class="gd-p">Two lines on To do keep an owner&#39;s money right without opening their page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Record the first and last month paid by &quot;: their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record what they paid</b>, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car&#39;s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. Never for a shareholder.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Enter the terms agreed with &quot;: their cars still use the standard grid. Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the terms</b>: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to change? Press <b class="gd-ui">Not needed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">These are correct</b>: the line does not come back.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-shareholder-s-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A shareholder&#39;s own car</h2><p class="gd-p">On the owner&#39;s page, each car has <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A shareholder&#39;s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-cancellation-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancellation refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: the refund for each cancellation tier.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When the renter cancels</th><th scope="col">Refund (default)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start</td><td>95%</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before the start</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before the start</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Under 24 hours, or after the start</td><td>0%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> sit under the name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Cars and terms: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> and History (see An owner&#39;s terms, car by car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender&#39;s permission of each car. <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason), <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes a car&#39;s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. Open a form and press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b> to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b>, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> puts a box&#39;s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under <b class="gd-ui">Every signature</b>. The step is done when every form is signed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b>: paste or upload the VINs, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car&#39;s terms, for each car whose terms are set.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Further down: <b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send a sign-in link to the owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A car&#39;s page has the same Government forms box (Owner &amp; documents).</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:410/1030"><img src="/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="410" height="1030"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.6%;top:4.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16.1%;top:32.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.5%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.2%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-terms-car-by-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s terms, car by car</h2><p class="gd-p">The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner&#39;s page and its Terms tab: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car&#39;s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not signed yet (or not approved yet): <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings &gt; Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days&#39; written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner&#39;s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car&#39;s History.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.</p><p class="gd-p">The same editor is on the car&#39;s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner&#39;s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-pay-an-owner-a-flat-monthly-amount" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an owner a flat monthly amount</h2><p class="gd-p">Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Flat monthly payment</b>, type the <b class="gd-ui">Amount a month</b> (for example 900.00), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b> and, if it ends, the <b class="gd-ui">Last day</b>. Write the Reason (kept in the history).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">From that date the owner&#39;s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Back to revenue share: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars&#39; own unless you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge to the owner</b> beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner&#39;s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-change-a-signed-car-s-management-mode" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change a signed car&#39;s Management Mode</h2><p class="gd-p">Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change mode</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">New Management Mode</b> and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b>, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked for this</b> only when it is their own request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars&#39; signature and the owner is emailed the notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else (CarmaCars&#39; own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw it</b> if needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-paid-and-signed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Paid and signed</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Paid and signed</b> tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checklist and quick actions</b>. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same checklist sits at the top of each owner&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with <b class="gd-ui">Waiting to sign</b> (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on &quot; in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner&#39;s documents.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Forms C and D</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars&#39; witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/470"><img src="/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="470"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:57.6%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-the-earnings-calculator-on-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The earnings calculator on List your car</h2><p class="gd-p">People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. Since release 48 the numbers are conservative and follow the season, and the result says plainly it is a rough estimate, not a promise.</p><p class="gd-p">They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the <b class="gd-ui">days rented in an average month</b> (4 to 22, 12 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, &quot;set in your agreement&quot;). The page then works a whole year, month by month:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A month&#39;s rented days are the days chosen times that month&#39;s factor: summer runs above the average, winter under it, and the shoulder months (spring and fall) are the slowest.</li><li>A rented day earns the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class&#39;s starting rate in Program settings) less a typical discount for weekly rates and offers.</li><li>Their share of that, less the monthly fees.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">It shows the average month, the year (the twelve months added up, never twelve of the best month), the range from the slowest month to the busiest, the rented days of each month as bars, and how many months the share would not cover the fees. &quot;Just cheaper insurance&quot; shows the fleet policy&#39;s fee and what they would keep in their slowest month.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown</b> and <b class="gd-ui">the monthly tracker fee shown</b>, in dollars a month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave either one empty and the page says &quot;Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement&quot; and shows the earnings &quot;before fees&quot;. No amount is ever made up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set both and the page takes them off every month and the year. Each owner&#39;s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the rented days of an average month it starts from</b> (12): keep it low, a new car takes months to fill.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The percent that comes off the listed daily rate on a rented day</b> (15).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The factor of each month</b> (jan to dec) against an average month (1.00): by default June 1.10, July and August 1.30, December 0.85, January and February 0.75, May and September 0.85, March and October 0.70, April and November 0.65. Every month must be there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-agreements-who-still-needs-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements: who still needs to sign</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Owners and partners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Agreements</b>. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line says <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sent, not signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not sent</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing</b>. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows &quot;invite first&quot;: press Invite on the Owners list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner&#39;s Terms tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>&quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot; marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-fleet-supplier-the-fleet-lease" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: the fleet lease</h2><p class="gd-p">For a supplier&#39;s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier route</b>. To agree other numbers, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the lease terms</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier on file without the route: press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the lease terms</b> and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the <b class="gd-ui">Upkeep Table</b>: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add each car with <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on the owner&#39;s page. The <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b> step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car already on file: press <b class="gd-ui">Put on the lease</b> beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b>, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car&#39;s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier&#39;s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">An upkeep cost: <b class="gd-ui">Record an upkeep cost</b>. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-approve-a-fleet-supplier-s-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve a fleet supplier&#39;s cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b> like any other, with each car&#39;s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b> beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check <b class="gd-ui">Delivered on</b> (the lease starts that day) and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows &quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot;. The default lease terms are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Owners &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner</b> offers the same route: choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. So does <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> for a new owner.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owner-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner rewards</b> shows the kits to ship, the upgrades to answer, each owner&#39;s months and code, and what the rewards cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A merch kit to ship: when an owner presses Redeem on their Rewards tab, the kit shows here and on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> with the address they confirmed. Ship it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark shipped</b> with the tracking number and what it cost. The owner is told and sees <b class="gd-ui">Shipped</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A free upgrade: when an owner&#39;s car is down for a repair they say CarmaCars caused, they ask here. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> with the amount CarmaCars covers (they get a one-time code), or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason they read.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a credit</b> gives an owner a credit by hand. Every credit is a line on the owner&#39;s next statement and an expense in the books (Owner rewards and credits, account 5310).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">What owners get: 20% off another car while theirs is out; a friends and family code (10% off a friend&#39;s first rental, and the owner earns the 20% kickback); $100 for referring an owner once the new car has been live 30 days; a merch kit at 6 months and a premium kit at 12; a $25 birthday rental credit; priority support and early access.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Every number is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner rewards</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">Program setting: Sign first (on). An owner&#39;s master agreement is made as soon as their profile is complete, with no car: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement for a fleet supplier, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. The owner signs it in the portal; CarmaCars countersigns at once with the signing officer of Settings.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Schedule A.</b> A supplier&#39;s car gets its numbered Schedule A entry when it is added (one at a time, or Add cars from a list of VINs with a tier and plate per row) and its government forms then. A program owner&#39;s car gets its entry when you set its terms. Cars added after the master is signed are confirmed by the owner with one signature per batch (the Additional Vehicle Schedule).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The gate.</b> A car is not approved (a supplier&#39;s application), delivered (put on the lease) or rented (live) until the master agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. Approving before the signature is kept: the application shows &quot;Approved, waiting for the signature&quot; and goes through by itself when the owner signs. If it cannot, you get a To do.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Agreements before cars.</b> The owner page and the application show exactly what is missing and who it waits on. Send reminder emails the owner (with the in-app notice and the push); once in 10 minutes at most.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding Method.</b> On the owner&#39;s Terms tab, Change the method corrects a car&#39;s method before its Vehicle Schedule is signed: the schedule, the plan and the government forms follow. The connector does the same with set_onboarding_method (previewed, then confirmed).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Document check</b> (Owners &gt; Document check, and the connector&#39;s owner_documents_check): anything still inconsistent on an owner&#39;s documents, by owner, with what fixes it: a signing officer title that is a name (titles are roles, such as Director), a method that does not fit how the car is held (with none chosen, a car starts on Transfer, never Co-Registrant), a first and last month off the rule (two months of the Insurance Fee, which never carries HST), an empty value on a schedule.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded.</b> A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded keeps its car presumed out after its return time: no new offer or booking goes on the car until you record the handover, the return or a no-show. Fleet gets the To do, then the Admins once the return time passed.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site. The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.
## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.
', 'Fleet', 'Field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews, similar cars and listings.',
  'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site. The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.
## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.

## Sign first, then cars

An owner''s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car''s Schedule A entry. On the owner''s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car''s tier and plate.

A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as "Pickup not recorded, car presumed out": record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-schedule-field-jobs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Schedule field jobs</h2><p class="gd-p">Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking&#39;s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day&#39;s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. &quot;Made from the booking&quot; marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Change a job with <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> (another shift), <b class="gd-ui">Assign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), <b class="gd-ui">Move</b> (time and place) or <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b>, the place filled in from the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings &gt; Program.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/fleet</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/565"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="565"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.9%;top:51.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Shifts, next seven days</b> shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (<b class="gd-ui">Jobs on it</b>). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Need more? Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>: the first day&#39;s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a person</b> puts someone on a shift and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking&#39;s real time; the renter&#39;s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> takes a job off its person and its shift; tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-missing-check-ins-and-check-outs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing check-ins and check-outs</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b> on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b> and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-fleet-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet map</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin&#39;s. Every staff member sees the cars&#39; positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Car map</b>), read only, and field staff under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car page and booking page shows <b class="gd-ui">Where the car is</b>: moving or parked, when it last reported and <b class="gd-ui">Open on the map</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>. Only Admins and fleet staff press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-hours" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field hours</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Field hours</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clocked in now</b> lists who is on, since when. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between pay periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock out: press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out for them</b>, set the time they finished and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Where they clocked in</h3><p class="gd-p">The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-daily-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Daily checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Daily checks</b> and choose <b class="gd-ui">Opening check</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Closing check</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the opening check</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Save the closing check</b>). You can save it again.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/checks</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/820"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.5%;top:15.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:44.7%;top:42%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:64.2%;top:94%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking press <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b>; on a booking on rent, <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Afterwards press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> and a reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-photo-reviews-after-a-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photo reviews after a return</h2><p class="gd-p">After each return, the field photo set waits under <b class="gd-ui">Photo reviews</b>. Compare it with the pickup set. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review done</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a re-shoot</b> if a photo is missing or unclear.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-similar-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Similar cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car&#39;s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> with a note when they are different cars, or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b> when they are.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/460"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="460"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">From a listing, press <b class="gd-ui">The car and its rates</b>, or open the car from Field jobs and its <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> for the kilometres, or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check What renters pay under the fields, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-listings-and-covering-plates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listings and covering plates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/340"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="340"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:54.5%;top:49.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The listing&#39;s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>: the editor opens under the photo; <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/776"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="776"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.6%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.5%;top:62.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:43.1%;top:92.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-missing-angles-and-short-videos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing angles and short videos</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press <b class="gd-ui">Make</b> and the angle (for example <b class="gd-ui">Make Rear</b>): the image model makes the view from the car&#39;s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make a short video</b> for a 9:16 video of the car&#39;s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-publish-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-in: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">An urgent To do &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot; means the renter pressed <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter&#39;s photos), then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> takes the VIN from the car: <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> in the door frame or under the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>; drag the extras into their order in the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo&#39;s edge is cut off by itself. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b>, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model&#39;s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b> does every car. Under a photo, <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again and <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before. <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b> on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>); the website&#39;s photos stay as they are. <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b> on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: <b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">With a model</b> (the image model&#39;s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or <b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b> (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-screen-many-photos-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One screen, many photos (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b> on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.</p><p class="gd-p">Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter&#39;s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car&#39;s page, record <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Return to owner</b> with photos: the owner sees them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-repair-costs-on-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repair costs on a car</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b>, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> prints that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-government-forms-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Government forms (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-odometer-and-fuel-at-every-check-in-and-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photo of the dashboard</b>: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Selfie in front of the car</b>: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking&#39;s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car&#39;s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-change-the-car-of-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change the car of a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b>, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car&#39;s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-an-accident-reported-by-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An accident reported by a renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-payments-and-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments and calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet takes payments on a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.</p><p class="gd-p">Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and <b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calls and texts</b> is your inbox. A car late back has <b class="gd-ui">Returning now</b> on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.</p><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> beside the form (who, when, the version) and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> and the owner is asked to sign again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-close-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Close ended trips</h2><p class="gd-p">A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has <b class="gd-ui">Mark settled (released by expiry)</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-the-primary-photo-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag <b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. <b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b>. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> card on Listings: each car&#39;s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b>. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-applicant-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field applicant calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. <b class="gd-ui">Field applicant calls</b> on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-value-and-fuel-on-the-car-page-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Value and fuel</b>:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Canadian Black Book value</b> (with the date checked) or an <b class="gd-ui">Estimated value (when no Black Book)</b>: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Tank (litres)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Fuel grade</b> (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or <b class="gd-ui">Battery (kWh)</b> for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-delivery-and-fuel-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The shift board shows each field person&#39;s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.</li><li>You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.</li><li>Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.</li><li>An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-every-view-generated-from-the-car-s-photos-release-47" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every view generated from the car&#39;s photos (release 47)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car&#39;s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged and the car&#39;s real photo of that angle stays on the site. The real photos stay on the car&#39;s record. On <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Generated set</b> shows each car&#39;s views made out of nine; <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> makes them again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-picked-up-deposit-pending-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open <b class="gd-ui">Let the car go with the deposit owed</b>, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now</b> has the box <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because</b>, and the check-in panel has <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it</b>. The booking then shows <b class="gd-ui">Deposit pending $X</b> everywhere. Each morning the renter&#39;s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-studio-renders-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio renders (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car&#39;s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.</li><li>Renders go live by themselves. You get &quot;Studio photos live&quot; in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.</li><li>Something is off: open the car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b>.</li><li>To render every published car now: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Render every published car</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-evidence-for-every-fee-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Evidence for every fee (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking&#39;s Money tab, <b class="gd-ui">Evidence for every fee</b> lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled &quot;Field:&quot; when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Attach evidence</b> on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a return charge</b>: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter&#39;s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-tracker-events-and-pound-flags-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b>, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car&#39;s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b>; you do not.</li><li>Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.</li><li>A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">A car that leaves Ontario or Canada</b>: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: a car parked at a known pound.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an urgent To do and alert. Open <b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: the lot&#39;s phone and hours are on the row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the path</b> and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), <b class="gd-ui">Recovered, nothing to charge</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not a pound</b>. Write what happened in a sentence.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b> are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot&#39;s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car&#39;s Schedule A entry. On the owner&#39;s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car&#39;s tier and plate.</p><p class="gd-p">A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as &quot;Pickup not recorded, car presumed out&quot;: record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 3801 END
